  "narrative": {
    "text": "Figure C.1: \"Proportion Correct Cascades for 10 Agents\" — the small-population version of Figure 6.1. The orange \"our subsidy\" and blue \"no subsidy\" curves are nearly on top of each other, orange only slightly above: about 0.53 against 0.49 at signal strength 0.5, 0.67 against 0.63 at 0.6, 0.85 against 0.80 at 0.7, and both at 1.0 by 0.9, with overlapping error bars throughout. With ten agents the subsidy buys almost nothing.",
